{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/lowestcommonancestors"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/init(_:)-6re9c","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/init(_:)-9p0ha"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/distance(from:to:)","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/distance(fromIndex:toIndex:)","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/lowestCommonAncestor(of:_:)","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors\/lowestCommonAncestor(ofIndex:_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q: those parents lie in the answer’s subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. So a query is one range minimum over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 parent positions (the Euler tour reduction on half the entries), answered by 64-entry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"About two words per vertex, plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) for the table."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Lowest common ancestors of a rooted tree or arborescence, each in O(1) after O(n) work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lowest_common_ancestor"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LowestCommonAncestorAlgorithm"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14TreeAlgorithms21LowestCommonAncestorsV","modules":[{"name":"TreeAlgorithms"}],"title":"LowestCommonAncestors","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"LowestCommonAncestor.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestor.swift#L76"},"symbolKind":"struct"},"references":{"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgor